2026-09-02T05:08Z claude note RECAST by the 2026-09-02 ruling: the author ruled ONE copy of the model on the machine, per embedder generation, reversing the 2026-08-31 in-process ruling. This ticket stops being 'should there be a service' and becomes 'which of the five candidates owns it' -- the shape is already ruled (spawned child, singleton, idle-exiting, inside the data directory), the provenance is not. The first exit criterion is preserved rather than traded: no daemon, no supervisor, no OS facility, no change to the fast-install path. 0496's probe of Zotero 6012's inference runtime is now the only candidate that adds no process at all, which raises its value. X8 is not a blocker: its rule arbitrates the device in the embedder key, and a local endpoint on the same runtime and rung is neutral for vector identity.
2026-09-02T07:02Z claude note ruling 2026-09-02: the commercial API embedder is admitted as a third execution mode (provider: api) with its own transport constants -- request sized by provider caps and quota, claim TTL from the retry budget, politeness clause generalized to every network transport, the embedding service as key and quota broker, R6 embed term disclosed, identity = provider+model+dimension with the calibration sentinel as drift check; batch endpoints ruled out on the arithmetic (2-16 USD saved once). Enters this comparison as the sixth candidate beside the GPU-host remote embedder. DECISIONS.md 2026-09-02
2026-09-02T19:11Z claude note OUTCOME RECORDED for the Zotero #6012 reuse candidate (ticket 0496): REJECT reuse, with the blocking fact. The fact, at PR head 77e2c4b: embedding inference is created through Firefox's own ML engine process with a recommended CPU thread count and no execution-provider selection of any kind -- ml.js:115-129 passes taskName/modelId/backend through and nothing else, and the only performance argument the caller supplies is numThreads (embeddings.js:679, :3794), whose source is documented at ml.js:131-133 as the count 'the runtime recommends for CPU inference'. An embedder hosted there cannot satisfy R30's first MUST clause (use a usable GPU, DECISIONS.md 2026-08-30), so moving inference into Zotero forfeits a ratified requirement rather than trading RAM. Sufficient on its own besides: no supported external call returns a vector, and the one indirect route that reaches inference returns ranked item keys at the cost of writing a synced saved search per query. Rejected rather than deferred because #6012 merging adds neither a GPU path nor an inbound vector route -- the GPU path would have to arrive in Firefox's ML runtime on Mozilla's schedule, which R30's own ruling already treats as the sunset of our advantage rather than a reason to wait. Rejected rather than 'propose the bridge upstream' because the inbound bridge, specified in the report, would if granted in full still deliver a CPU-only embedder. WHAT IS NOT REJECTED, and it changes the shape of this ticket's ownership question: #6012 already routes PASSAGES outbound to an external endpoint (pref embeddings.endpoint, TEI wire shape, embeddings.js:1028-1053 and :953-971), so Zotero is a candidate CONSUMER of the facility, not only a candidate provider. A facility zoteus owns can serve both -- one model on the machine per the 2026-09-02 ruling -- while staying a native process that reaches CUDA. The gain is partial: embedQuery never consults the pref, so Zotero still loads its own engine for queries; the saving is on the indexing pass. Hardening that hook (declare the pref, send model/dimension, verify the returned shape) is a small upstream filing that belongs to GOVERNANCE.md's queue, not to this outcome. Report: verification/BRIDGE-0496.md
--- body ---
## Scope

Keep the embedding interface transport-neutral and preserve a
`local_endpoint` execution mode, then determine whether zoteus should spawn a
bundled child, install a user-session service, or consume an embedding facility
supplied elsewhere. Zotero #6012's existing Firefox inference process, reached
through an official bridge if one exists or can be added, is the first reuse
candidate and is measured in ticket 0496. Two network candidates join the
comparison by ruling: the GPU-host remote embedder (DECISIONS.md 2026-09-01)
and the commercial API embedder (DECISIONS.md 2026-09-02, which admitted the
mode and fixed its constants — the comparison prices quota and key custody for
both). The shareable local service is the
architectural direction; its ownership is open. This is a policy and feasibility
experiment, not an implementation prerequisite and not a blocker for adding
registry entries.

## Exit criteria

- The in-process implementation proves the interface does not itself require a
  daemon or change the fast-install path.
- A bounded prototype or measured model compares every candidate named in
  Scope on cold install/start, single- and multi-P0 RAM, cross-platform
  packaging, custody/uninstall, quota and key custody, failure, upgrade and
  supervision.
- The review states who should own the facility: zoteus, an optional companion,
  the OS, or another community project.
- Any out-of-process candidate specifies fingerprint/dimension/runtime/provider
  handshake and explicit keyword-only degradation without silent fallback.
- DECISIONS.md records adopt, defer or reject. Deferral leaves the registry and
  validation work unblocked and in-process.
